No luck, tried 2 variations:

```
{
    "rules": {
        "quotes": [1, "single"],
        "no-unused-vars": 1
    },
    "ecmaFeatures": {
        "modules": true,
        "blockBindings": true
    }
}
```

and

```
{
    "rules": {
        "quotes": [1, "single"],
        "no-unused-vars": 1
    },
    "env":{
        "es6": true
    },
    "ecmaFeatures": {
        "modules": true,
        "blockBindings": true
    }
}
```

@fczuardi using `ecmaFeatures.module` is the same as using `ecmaFeatures.qwersdfasfe`. Here's the source code from espree.js:

```
    var allowClasses = extra.ecmaFeatures.classes,
        allowModules = extra.ecmaFeatures.modules,
        allowBlockBindings = extra.ecmaFeatures.blockBindings;
```

It looks for `modules` here, not `module`.

@extesy here is the check:

https://github.com/eslint/eslint/blob/master/lib/eslint.js#L655

maybe your bug is unrelated, but `ecmaFeatures.qwersdfasfe` is definitely not the same as `ecmaFeatures.module` :)
